# FS02-060: registry-v0 is PR-based and operator-merged. There is no self-service write
# path at v0 — every change to the registry, the ledger, or the CT log is reviewed and
# merged by the steward operator.
#
# [HUMAN TODO] Replace the placeholder team with the real one once the GitHub org exists
# and branch protection is configured. A CODEOWNERS file naming a team that does not
# exist silently reviews nothing, which is worse than no file: GitHub cannot request a
# review from a non-existent owner, so a "required review from Code Owners" rule can be
# satisfied by nobody at all. Verify on the org's first PR that a review is actually
# requested.

*                       @purposesource/stewards

# The three append-only trees. Same owner today; called out separately because the review
# question is different — for these the reviewer is checking that nothing EARLIER changed,
# which is a different read from reviewing a new registry entry.
/ledger/                @purposesource/stewards
/ct/                    @purposesource/stewards
/registry/              @purposesource/stewards

# The contracts and the gates. A change here changes what the data is allowed to be.
/schema/                @purposesource/stewards
/scripts/               @purposesource/stewards
/config/                @purposesource/stewards
/.github/               @purposesource/stewards
